WEBVTT

00:00.930 --> 00:01.980
Prepare yourself!

00:03.180 --> 00:05.230
Lightning Strike!

00:08.820 --> 00:09.820
It's over!

00:09.820 --> 00:11.930
The winner is Ariane Algren.

00:51.850 --> 00:52.960
Sir?

00:57.810 --> 00:59.260
Master?

00:59.260 --> 01:00.230
Abbie?

01:00.230 --> 01:01.410
Ray!

01:02.080 --> 01:05.460
And who are these people with you?

01:05.460 --> 01:07.180
So you've noticed.

01:07.180 --> 01:09.580
Let me first tell you about the Hail family.

01:10.120 --> 01:11.580
The Hail family?

01:11.830 --> 01:16.010
Their bloodline has been responsible 
for the kingdom's intelligence agency.

01:16.390 --> 01:18.940
The dedicated maid for your beautiful master

01:18.940 --> 01:23.090
is actually one of the kingdom's 
best intelligence agents.

01:23.090 --> 01:25.150
Miss Carla is an intelligence agent?

01:25.800 --> 01:30.220
I can't believe you called 
yourself beautiful, Lydia!

01:26.130 --> 01:29.700
Thank you for looking after 
my little brother, Ray.

01:29.700 --> 01:30.990
Your little brother?

01:30.990 --> 01:31.770
That's me.

01:32.750 --> 01:36.080
Our club leader is Carla's little brother?!

01:36.080 --> 01:37.820
I am Lex Hail.

01:37.820 --> 01:40.720
With that revealed, nice to meet you again.

01:40.720 --> 01:42.390
L-Likewise.

01:42.390 --> 01:43.660
Let's get to business.

01:44.100 --> 01:47.490
The Grim Reapers have infiltrated 
the Magic Chevalier.

01:44.360 --> 01:46.340
Dumbpink...

01:46.340 --> 01:47.490
Beh.

01:47.490 --> 01:52.670
Their aim is to kidnap the daughters of 
the top noble houses, or murder them.

01:52.670 --> 01:53.500
That's where you come in.

01:53.840 --> 01:55.890
I want you to be vigilant, as well.

01:55.890 --> 01:58.620
Since they are targeting students,

01:58.620 --> 02:01.160
the probability that you will 
encounter them is high.

02:01.160 --> 02:02.510
Understood.

02:02.510 --> 02:03.510
I'm sorry about this.

02:03.900 --> 02:06.150
Lex is in charge of student security.

02:06.610 --> 02:09.140
If anything happens, he can help you.

02:09.480 --> 02:11.650
I'm counting on you, Ray.

02:12.970 --> 02:14.640
Don't let your guard down.

02:14.640 --> 02:17.860
If push comes to shove, 
you can use that, too.

02:15.250 --> 02:17.290
Hey, Lydia!

02:18.290 --> 02:19.580
Eek!

02:18.620 --> 02:19.580
Understood!

02:22.050 --> 02:23.630
<i>The Aywell Empire.</i>

02:25.080 --> 02:26.450
<i>The Grim Reapers.</i>

02:27.870 --> 02:30.250
<i>You will not get in the way 
of Amelia and the others.</i>

02:30.990 --> 02:33.640
<i>I'll stake my name on it 
as the Iceblade Sorcerer.</i>

03:01.990 --> 03:05.740
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

04:04.760 --> 04:07.970
<b>Episode 8
The Boy Who Became the World's Strongest Sorcerer Inspires the Rose</b>

04:08.830 --> 04:10.960
The match is over!

04:10.960 --> 04:13.510
With that, the beautiful 
goddess Rebecca Bradley,

04:13.530 --> 04:15.590
a third-year student of the 
Arnold Academy of Sorcery,

04:15.590 --> 04:19.060
has just advanced to the final 
round of the main bracket!

04:19.060 --> 04:22.320
Last year's champion really 
showed us what she can do!

04:22.320 --> 04:24.050
She's so strong! So strong!

04:24.050 --> 04:26.030
And so beautiful!

04:26.030 --> 04:28.620
She's the ultimate magic sword fighter!

04:28.620 --> 04:31.460
Lady Rebecca will probably 
be champion again this year!

04:31.460 --> 04:33.540
Actually, nothing else makes sense!

04:33.900 --> 04:39.050
The next match will be 
Arnold Academy of Sorcery's Lurio Fuchia

04:36.650 --> 04:39.050
Rebecca really is amazing.

04:39.050 --> 04:42.760
versus Mercross Academy of 
Sorcery's Lucas Forst!

04:39.280 --> 04:40.240
She is.

04:40.740 --> 04:41.950
Ray?

04:43.020 --> 04:44.000
What's wrong?

04:45.850 --> 04:48.770
Well you see... Amelia is...

04:49.080 --> 04:50.750
Did something happen to her?

04:51.040 --> 04:53.240
She won't come out of her room.

04:53.240 --> 04:56.340
She says it's fatigue from yesterday, but...

04:56.730 --> 04:59.690
Her voice sounds like she's suffering...

04:59.690 --> 05:02.850
She won't tell us anything...

05:02.850 --> 05:05.080
We're worried about her.

05:05.850 --> 05:07.120
I see...

05:07.120 --> 05:08.010
Ray.

05:08.460 --> 05:10.400
Match over!

05:10.400 --> 05:11.740
The match is over!

05:11.740 --> 05:14.490
And what an unbelievable record!

05:14.490 --> 05:16.870
The winner is Lucas Forst!

05:16.870 --> 05:19.770
The match only took two seconds!

05:19.770 --> 05:23.130
This is a record-breaking time 
here at the Magic Chevalier!

05:23.510 --> 05:26.530
An incredible dark horse 
has just revealed himself!

05:26.530 --> 05:28.450
T-Two seconds?!

05:28.450 --> 05:30.550
Lucas Forst...

05:30.980 --> 05:33.060
He's a second-year from Mercross.

05:42.990 --> 05:45.500
There're some crazy people out there.

06:08.590 --> 06:10.850
That's the spirit.

06:10.850 --> 06:13.010
You're amazing!

06:13.010 --> 06:15.250
Father, Tiana.

06:15.250 --> 06:16.350
Here.

06:16.350 --> 06:18.150
Thank you, Tiana.

06:18.150 --> 06:20.220
We'll have to fix that again.

06:20.650 --> 06:23.120
I'm so sorry, father.

06:24.040 --> 06:25.640
Don't worry about it!

06:25.640 --> 06:27.900
I'm looking forward to 
tomorrow's competition.

06:28.770 --> 06:30.560
I will definitely win.

06:41.130 --> 06:42.460
Why don't you go?

06:42.460 --> 06:43.220
Huh?

06:49.890 --> 06:51.630
Elisa. Claris.

06:52.540 --> 06:53.710
Ray.

06:54.410 --> 06:57.250
Please help Amelia.

06:57.250 --> 07:00.700
You're the only one who can help her now.

07:00.700 --> 07:01.690
Yes.

07:02.140 --> 07:05.400
I'll go tell her what I'm thinking.

07:11.000 --> 07:12.080
Amelia!

07:12.360 --> 07:14.820
It's me, Ray White!

07:15.660 --> 07:17.720
You don't have to come out. Just listen.

07:19.860 --> 07:23.310
I was... afraid.

07:25.080 --> 07:27.310
Afraid to step into your heart.

07:28.110 --> 07:30.180
I worried that if I got 
too close to your heart,

07:30.700 --> 07:34.430
I might accidentally break it.

07:36.120 --> 07:38.670
I kept asking myself if my 
decision had been the right one.

07:39.160 --> 07:45.070
So I kept running away 
from really facing you.

07:46.520 --> 07:49.400
Amelia, I want you to tell me.

07:49.840 --> 07:51.860
I want to know your heart!

07:51.860 --> 07:53.040
Your heart...

07:53.570 --> 07:54.970
I want to touch it.

08:05.070 --> 08:06.120
Come in.

08:11.430 --> 08:15.730
I really am hopeless.

08:16.600 --> 08:19.670
You see, all I've done this whole time

08:19.670 --> 08:22.990
is play-act everyone's 
expectation of Amelia Rose.

08:23.470 --> 08:26.770
Without any prompting, I imagined 
everyone else's image of me,

08:26.770 --> 08:28.060
and played the part.

08:28.590 --> 08:32.120
All to become a me that's worthy 
of being House Rose's eldest.

08:32.920 --> 08:38.790
And I tried, and tried, 
and tried, and tried,

08:38.790 --> 08:40.720
and got this far.

08:42.370 --> 08:46.520
But compared to everything 
you've been through,

08:46.520 --> 08:48.910
it's a big pile of nothing, isn't it?

08:49.650 --> 08:54.020
There's no point in comparing 
people's pasts, or their suffering.

08:54.020 --> 09:00.010
However, it's certain that you've been 
trying hard, despite all the suffering.

09:00.010 --> 09:00.870
Isn't that true?

09:02.370 --> 09:05.510
Yes. You're right.

09:06.130 --> 09:07.340
For so long...

09:08.080 --> 09:09.740
I've been hurting for so long...

09:10.340 --> 09:11.690
I've suffered.

09:12.350 --> 09:19.290
I've always wondered why I kept 
on living when it hurt so badly.

09:20.180 --> 09:23.800
Then I met everyone! I met you!

09:23.800 --> 09:25.990
I thought that I could 
actually attain something!

09:26.920 --> 09:31.810
If I won this competition, 
I could finally be someone.

09:31.810 --> 09:33.390
That's what I was thinking, and yet...

09:37.160 --> 09:40.430
I can't beat Ariane.

09:42.810 --> 09:45.040
No matter how much time passes,

09:45.730 --> 09:48.080
I'll never be anything but a bird in a cage.

09:48.760 --> 09:50.130
Why?!

09:50.130 --> 09:52.010
Why am I alive?!

09:52.440 --> 09:55.140
I pretend, play the role of "me",

09:55.140 --> 09:57.450
trying to materialize the 
ideal version of myself,

09:57.450 --> 10:00.020
but I still can't catch up to her!

10:00.020 --> 10:03.330
Does this kind of life 
even have any meaning?

10:03.330 --> 10:05.600
Tell me, Ray!

10:05.600 --> 10:09.600
Why am I alive?

10:11.730 --> 10:17.690
Amelia, being alive has no meaning in itself.

10:19.170 --> 10:22.630
There is no meaning to our existence.

10:26.470 --> 10:27.600
But still!

10:31.210 --> 10:35.360
But we, us humans, we can 
find a reason to live!

10:35.930 --> 10:39.210
You can create your own 
reason for being alive.

10:40.860 --> 10:43.690
Create... a reason?

10:44.000 --> 10:45.460
Crying, laughing,

10:45.890 --> 10:47.920
sorrows and joy,

10:47.920 --> 10:51.170
sharing all that with your friends 
and supporting each other in life.

10:52.200 --> 10:54.900
Won't that do as your reason to live?

11:00.400 --> 11:04.520
I want to keep living, next to you.

11:06.110 --> 11:07.140
Really?

11:07.650 --> 11:09.870
You don't mind having me around,

11:10.610 --> 11:13.030
even when I'm weak like this?

11:13.030 --> 11:13.970
I don't.

11:14.730 --> 11:17.520
That is the real Amelia Rose, isn't it?

11:40.920 --> 11:42.040
Now, then...

11:43.540 --> 11:44.590
Amelia?

12:15.370 --> 12:18.260
It's okay, Amelia.

12:18.260 --> 12:20.160
I believe in you.

12:20.160 --> 12:21.510
I know you can win.

12:23.260 --> 12:25.450
Good night, Amelia.

12:29.020 --> 12:30.500
Today we will be conducting

12:30.500 --> 12:33.260
the final match for the rookie 
bracket of the Magic Chevalier!

12:34.000 --> 12:38.900
The contestants crossing blades will 
be Ariane Algren and Amelia Rose!

12:39.390 --> 12:42.880
Interestingly, this will be a match between 
daughters of the great three noble houses!

12:42.880 --> 12:45.290
Which of the two will be victorious?

12:46.150 --> 12:50.510
The arena is fired up before 
the match has even begun!

12:51.580 --> 12:52.820
I'm sorry I'm late.

12:52.820 --> 12:53.670
Ray.

12:53.670 --> 12:56.250
Ray, where is Amelia?

12:56.520 --> 12:57.910
She's fine now.

12:57.910 --> 12:58.740
Really?

12:59.000 --> 13:00.450
You did it, Ray!

13:00.450 --> 13:02.870
Only because you had my back.

13:02.870 --> 13:05.760
No, you're the one who did it.

13:05.760 --> 13:07.090
Where's Claris?

13:07.090 --> 13:09.270
She said she had to do some 
organizational staff work.

13:09.270 --> 13:12.270
I think she should be back soon.

13:12.270 --> 13:16.130
I see. I'll have to thank her later, too.

13:16.520 --> 13:19.470
I'm really glad it all worked out, though.

13:19.470 --> 13:24.080
I was worried about whether Amelia 
would be able to get some proper sleep.

13:24.080 --> 13:26.390
You don't have to worry about that.

13:26.390 --> 13:27.060
Huh?

13:27.060 --> 13:30.380
I spent the whole night with her.

13:30.380 --> 13:31.550
What?!

13:31.550 --> 13:33.660
All... night?

13:33.660 --> 13:36.610
Yes. She got plenty of sleep.

13:36.610 --> 13:38.740
So you were there until morning?!

13:38.740 --> 13:39.990
Yes?

13:41.140 --> 13:44.260
Anyway, I'll go give Amelia her rose now.

13:45.480 --> 13:50.030
I can't believe Ray would climb the 
steps to adulthood so casually...

13:50.030 --> 13:52.040
I don't think that happened, Evi.

13:52.040 --> 13:52.760
Huh?

13:53.090 --> 13:55.110
It's the same as always!

13:55.110 --> 13:57.120
I mean, we're talking about Ray here!

13:57.120 --> 14:00.960
Jeez, he always shocks me!

14:00.960 --> 14:02.280
What?

14:04.770 --> 14:09.030
I can't believe the organization 
work took until now!

14:09.030 --> 14:11.800
I'm not going to make it to Amelia's match!

14:21.360 --> 14:22.670
It's almost time.

14:23.380 --> 14:24.180
Yes.

14:29.250 --> 14:30.960
You're fine now.

14:31.470 --> 14:35.010
Ray, so... Well...

14:35.980 --> 14:43.240
Could I... Could I get another hug?

14:43.490 --> 14:45.230
Of course.

14:49.190 --> 14:50.440
I'll get going, then.

14:52.090 --> 14:53.210
Right.

14:53.210 --> 14:55.400
If anyone can win, it's you, Amelia.

14:55.830 --> 14:56.590
Yes.

15:00.920 --> 15:02.210
My apologies, Sera.

15:02.210 --> 15:02.950
Huh?

15:02.950 --> 15:04.570
Something urgent has come up.

15:04.570 --> 15:07.200
Now? But the match is about to start.

15:07.200 --> 15:08.410
I really do apologize.

15:08.680 --> 15:09.890
I'm counting on you.

15:09.890 --> 15:11.670
Hey, wait up!

15:19.830 --> 15:20.560
Sir.

15:20.840 --> 15:24.350
Claris Cleveland, the daughter 
of a high noble family,

15:24.350 --> 15:27.080
has gone missing alongside
eight other noble students.

15:27.440 --> 15:29.570
I will head below.

15:29.570 --> 15:30.580
Below?

15:30.580 --> 15:33.310
I feel something ominous from there.

15:33.310 --> 15:34.360
I see.

15:34.360 --> 15:38.120
Then I will check in with Lydia and 
the others first before joining you.

15:38.120 --> 15:39.380
Understood.

15:40.130 --> 15:42.820
Caro caro!

15:42.820 --> 15:44.370
Sorry I kept you waiting!

15:44.370 --> 15:47.080
Miss Carol, where were you?

15:47.400 --> 15:49.300
On. A. Date.

15:51.250 --> 15:52.790
And we are back!

15:52.790 --> 15:54.340
Youch, so cold!

15:54.340 --> 15:57.490
We will now commence the final 
match of the rookie bracket!

15:58.860 --> 16:01.850
It's finally time, Amelia.

16:01.850 --> 16:02.870
Indeed.

16:03.720 --> 16:05.860
I will be winning this.

16:05.860 --> 16:08.040
No, I will.

16:08.590 --> 16:11.110
Then, let's settle this!

16:11.110 --> 16:12.110
Let's!

16:12.110 --> 16:13.910
And the match has begun!

16:16.430 --> 16:19.670
It looks like competitor Algren 
has thrown her sword away!

16:23.110 --> 16:24.160
Ogre!

16:27.180 --> 16:29.910
Why don't we begin at full power?

16:38.690 --> 16:39.940
That's...

16:39.940 --> 16:41.560
...the same move she used to defeat Albert.

16:41.790 --> 16:43.630
An absurd display of speed!

16:43.630 --> 16:45.980
What kind of sorcery is that?

16:45.980 --> 16:50.080
That is one of her original spells.

16:50.510 --> 16:54.020
It's a bit amazing that she has specialized 
so much on the physical aspect.

16:55.330 --> 16:58.610
I'm not done yet, Amelia!

17:10.570 --> 17:11.680
Sister!

17:18.860 --> 17:21.310
This... Is it really...?

17:25.080 --> 17:26.440
I will...

17:27.500 --> 17:29.280
never lose!

17:34.040 --> 17:35.080
Claris!

17:37.470 --> 17:39.300
Are you all right?

17:45.470 --> 17:47.380
A huge stag beetle!

17:47.800 --> 17:50.140
Claris, are you hurt?

17:50.140 --> 17:51.580
H-Huh?

17:52.370 --> 17:55.200
How did I get here?

17:56.370 --> 17:57.740
What is this?

17:57.740 --> 17:59.870
It's a wide-area interference spell.

17:59.870 --> 18:00.960
They've begun.

18:00.960 --> 18:02.470
Wide-area interference?

18:02.810 --> 18:03.650
That's right.

18:04.140 --> 18:06.770
This area is now shut off 
from the outside world.

18:08.210 --> 18:10.030
They must be the Grim Reapers.

18:10.030 --> 18:12.290
Who are these guys?!

18:12.290 --> 18:13.760
Claris, I'm sorry.

18:13.760 --> 18:15.290
Huh? What!

18:15.290 --> 18:17.600
Wait, Ray. Ray!

18:17.600 --> 18:19.900
Don't speak for a while.

18:19.900 --> 18:23.740
M-M-My skirt!

18:22.110 --> 18:24.460
Chronos Lock, release!

18:25.440 --> 18:27.160
No!

18:27.470 --> 18:28.810
Icicle Blades!

18:28.810 --> 18:30.520
Huh, what?!

18:30.520 --> 18:32.180
This can't be happening...

18:32.180 --> 18:34.700
No!

18:35.180 --> 18:37.270
Claris, you're going to 
bite your own tongue off!

18:37.270 --> 18:39.760
But... but!

18:43.510 --> 18:45.060
Now what?

18:46.780 --> 18:47.980
Ray?

18:47.980 --> 18:49.050
It's fine.

19:05.920 --> 19:09.800
What on earth just happened?

19:09.800 --> 19:12.060
Huh?

19:12.060 --> 19:14.260
<i>Anti-Material Field.</i>

19:14.260 --> 19:15.460
Oh, Ray.

19:17.070 --> 19:18.510
You're not getting away!

19:18.510 --> 19:19.880
Diamond Dust!

19:27.690 --> 19:29.650
Wow!

19:29.650 --> 19:32.040
It's like a world of ice.

19:32.480 --> 19:34.410
Ray, is it over?

19:34.410 --> 19:36.900
It is. I didn't kill them.

19:37.180 --> 19:38.810
I see.

19:38.810 --> 19:40.440
You can leave the rest of this to us.

19:40.880 --> 19:43.120
Isn't there someone waiting for you?

19:43.120 --> 19:44.580
Thank you.

19:44.580 --> 19:45.700
Hey!

19:45.700 --> 19:49.700
Put me down first!

19:50.010 --> 19:53.350
The final match of the rookie 
bracket, Algren vs Rose.

19:53.350 --> 19:56.530
Neither contestant is backing down!
Both of them continue to trade blows!

19:58.170 --> 20:01.560
I will be using the ace up my sleeve!

20:02.660 --> 20:06.620
Ogre Scintilla!

20:08.960 --> 20:13.340
Player Algren is sparking 
to an unprecedented degree!

20:13.340 --> 20:14.730
Father...

20:14.730 --> 20:17.800
She's unleashed all of her bzz bzz!

20:17.800 --> 20:19.500
Ariane!

20:21.480 --> 20:26.070
Player Algren has gotten even shinier!

20:26.790 --> 20:30.090
So this is the true form of 
Ariane's original spell.

20:30.090 --> 20:32.870
Unbelievable. She could get even stronger?!

20:33.430 --> 20:35.370
Here I come!

20:41.070 --> 20:42.210
You're too slow.

20:47.030 --> 20:50.190
Explosions are nothing!

20:50.190 --> 20:52.410
If they can't hit me!

21:10.380 --> 21:12.990
R-Rose is down!

21:12.990 --> 21:15.180
Is this going to be the end?!

21:15.180 --> 21:18.290
It's over, Amelia.

21:19.820 --> 21:22.600
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

21:23.170 --> 21:25.920
<i>I'm going to lose.</i>

21:27.030 --> 21:29.520
<i>I really don't want to lose,</i>

21:30.110 --> 21:34.380
<i>but my body won't move.</i>

21:34.680 --> 21:35.890
Amelia!

21:35.120 --> 21:36.740
Amelia.

21:35.920 --> 21:37.310
Amelia.

21:38.210 --> 21:41.970
I want to keep living, next to you.

21:44.360 --> 21:46.610
Amelia!

21:46.960 --> 21:49.410
Get up!

21:52.370 --> 21:54.380
Prima materia encoding

21:53.160 --> 21:55.350
material code decoding

21:54.670 --> 21:56.500
material code processing

21:54.900 --> 21:57.110
αἰτία hū́lē eîdos 
efficient télos embodiment

21:57.110 --> 21:57.880
Causality.

22:01.010 --> 22:01.880
What is this?

22:02.570 --> 22:03.720
This is...

22:05.210 --> 22:10.400
Ariane, you can no longer reach me.

22:12.380 --> 22:13.750
Amelia...

22:16.990 --> 22:18.690
Butterfly Effect.

23:49.990 --> 23:54.990
<b>The Iceblade <b>Sorcerer
</b>Shall <b>Rule </b>the <b>World</b></b>

23:49.990 --> 23:54.990
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

23:49.990 --> 23:54.990
<b>~ Next Episode Preview ~</b>

23:50.230 --> 23:51.630
This is the preview of the next episode

23:51.630 --> 23:54.110
of <i>The Iceblade Sorcerer 
Shall Rule the World</i>!

23:55.000 --> 23:58.370
Crimson butterflies dance, azure 
lightning surges, and the battle rages on.

23:58.370 --> 24:02.460
The two souls that parted ways that day 
relentlessly speak through their fists.

24:02.460 --> 24:06.570
